          "title": "Big News",
          "description": "Añade información con oraciones de relativo explicativas: which, who, whose, most of whom. Incluye el test final de B2.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "big_news_lesson",
              "title": "Non-defining relative clauses",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Big news",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "I have some news. Harbour Studio, which I started twenty years ago in my kitchen, is going to change."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Change how?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "I'm retiring at the end of the year. My husband, who has been very patient, wants us to travel."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Helen, that's wonderful. But what will happen to the studio?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "That's the question. I've had an offer from Mark Reed, whose company wants to buy us."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Mark Reed? Our Mark?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "Yes. But there's another option, which I prefer. Lucía, can I speak to you after the meeting?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "Daniel tells me you've been thinking about starting your own studio, which doesn't surprise me at all."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "He told you? Oh no… I was going to tell you myself."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "Don't worry. I'd like you to take over some of our clients, most of whom already ask for you by name."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Me? Take over your clients?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "Think about it. You'd have your own studio, and the work I care about would be in good hands."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I… I don't know what to say."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "Say you'll think about it. That's all I ask."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "June. Helen calls the whole team into the meeting room. She looks emotional."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"Harbour Studio, which I started twenty years ago, is going to change.\" The part between commas…",
                        "options": [
                          "adds extra information",
                          "tells us which studio"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"My husband, who has been very patient…\" Could we use that instead of who?",
                        "options": [
                          "No, not between commas",
                          "Yes"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Mark Reed, whose company wants to buy us…\" Whose = …",
                        "options": [
                          "cuyo/a",
                          "quien"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"most of whom already ask for you\" Whom refers to…",
                        "options": [
                          "the clients",
                          "Lucía"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Non-defining relative clauses",
                    "explanation": "Las oraciones de relativo explicativas añaden información extra sobre algo que ya está identificado. Van entre comas y:\n• no admiten that: Harbour Studio, which I started… (nunca «, that I started»)\n• no se puede omitir el pronombre.\n\nWhich puede referirse a toda la frase anterior: You want your own studio, which doesn't surprise me (= lo cual).\n\nCon cuantificadores: most of whom (personas), some of which (cosas): our clients, most of whom ask for you by name.\n\nSon muy frecuentes en registro formal y escrito.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Uso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "who (personas)",
                          "My husband, who has been very patient, wants to travel."
                        ],
                        [
                          "which (cosas)",
                          "Harbour Studio, which I started in my kitchen, is going to change."
                        ],
                        [
                          "whose (posesión)",
                          "Mark Reed, whose company wants to buy us, made an offer."
                        ],
                        [
                          "which (toda la frase anterior)",
                          "You want your own studio, which doesn't surprise me."
                        ],
                        [
                          "most of whom / some of which",
                          "our clients, most of whom ask for you by name"
                        ],
                        [
                          "¡Nunca that ni omisión!",
                          "✗ Harbour Studio, that I started…"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Harbour Studio, which I started twenty years ago in my kitchen, is going to change.",
                      "My husband, who has been very patient, wants us to travel.",
                      "I've had an offer from Mark Reed, whose company wants to buy us.",
                      "I'd like you to take over some of our clients, most of whom already ask for you by name."
                    ]
                  }
